# oracle: fix bond/create iparam/jparam limits with new types (bead-spring melt: 16 chains of 8 beads, periodic 7.5^3 box, generated by a script; chain ends (bondcount 1 < 2) bond within 1.5, prob 0.5 with seed 4321, nevery 5, 500 steps). Each end that reaches 2 bonds changes type 1 to 2. Native: b332f28 (installed lmp, MC package included).
# Engine vs this fixture (Node 24; Node 20 gives the same numbers to the digits shown): 13 bonds made (f_c[2] = 13, bonds 112 -> 125), identical counts on every row. Max errors over the 11 rows: thermo rel 6.6e-11 (press; abs 3.1e-12), atoms rel 6.4e-9 (fz, abs 2.0e-9; the rest below 1e-9). A diagnostic variant (nevery 1, thermo every step, 160 steps; not part of the case) agrees with native to 1e-9 on every row.
# Native prints "Inconsistent image flags" for this run (the melt data carry no image flags and a few chains cross the periodic boundary); the engine uses the same closest-image bonds.
# oracle-inputs: w139bc_melt.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units lj
boundary p p p
atom_style bond
read_data w139bc_melt.data extra/bond/per/atom 2
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff * * 1.0 1.0
bond_style harmonic
bond_coeff 1 100.0 1.0
special_bonds lj/coul 0.0 1.0 1.0
neighbor 0.3 bin
velocity all create 1.0 4928 mom yes rot no dist gaussian
fix 1 all nve
fix c all bond/create 5 1 1 1.5 1 iparam 2 2 jparam 2 2 prob 0.5 4321
timestep 0.005
thermo_style custom step temp pe ebond press bonds f_c[1] f_c[2]
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 50
run 500
